  "did_you_know": "Satyrs, or lustful, drunken woodland gods, are the biggest partiers in ancient Greek mythology.",
  "early_education_description": null,
  "artlens_description": null,
  "description": "Part man and part beast, satyrs were mythical woodland creatures. In art, they were depicted with the ears and tail of a goat or horse, sometimes with hooves, and in a high state of sexual arousal. Satyrs often accompanied Dionysus, the god of wine, in his drinking bouts and other escapades. These three probably once decorated the rim of a large punch-bowl-shaped vessel for serving wine.",
